1) If you have sinned, ask for forgiveness immediately;
2) Do not try to hide your sin from God. He saw and heard everything.
3) When you repent, name the sin you have committed. Say specifically what you repent of

Would you be free from the burden of sin?
There’s power in the blood, power in the blood;
Would you o’er evil a victory win?
There’s wonderful power in the blood.
There is power, power, wonder-working power
In the blood of the Lamb;
There is power, power, wonder-working power
In the precious blood of the Lamb.
Would you be free from your passion and pride?
There’s power in the blood, power in the blood;
Come for a cleansing to Calvary’s tide;
There’s wonderful power in the blood.

1) When we pray, God will hear us;
2) When we preach, people will receive
salvation;
3) Some people will receive visible healing;
4) The lives of many people will be completely
changed;
5) The circumstances will depend on us instead
of us depending on them;
6) Our life will be filled with meaning and vision;
7) We will learn to communicate with Him.

1. In a home church, people have fellowship with one another (there are 5-10 people in a home church);
2. In a home church, people drink tea together to form a natural, family atmosphere;
3. In a home church, people serve one another with counsel, prayer, gifts of the Holy Spirit, and support;
4. In a home church, people grow by sharing insights from Sunday service sermons;
5. In a home church, people worship God in songs, prayers, and gifts of the Holy Spirit;
6. In a home church, people serve non-believers by helping them come to Christ.

Thus, we can live by faith in:
1) The Blood of Jesus (which cleanses us);
2) The holiness of Jesus (the power to win);
3) The righteousness of Jesus (the ability to live);
4) The love of Jesus (the ability to love).

1) trust;
2) contract (receipt);
3) payment.

1. To pray and intercede in tongues when the Holy Spirit drives us;
2. To speak with the Holy Spirit through our renewed spirit;
3. To use the gifts of the Spirit in ministry as a powerful weapon of God.
4. To, having received the power of the Spirit, bring lost people back to Christ.
